@startuml Emulator State Machine

[*] --> Initializing

state Initializing
Initializing: entry/fingerprint system
Initializing: entry/read RAM from bus
Initializing: entry/initialize CPU

state Resetting
Resetting: entry/reset CPU
Resetting: entry/stop E clock

state Running
Running: entry/start E clock
Running: do/bus sync, execute instruction

state Halted
Halted: entry/stop E clock

state Paused

state Loading
Loading: entry/stop E clock

state WaitingForInterrupt

Initializing --> Resetting : EVT_INIT

Resetting --> Running : EVT_POLL\n(!interrupt == INT_RESET)
Resetting --> Halted : EV_CMD_HALT
Resetting --> Running : EV_CMD_RUN
Resetting --> Resetting : EVT_POLL\n(interrupt == INT_RESET)

Running --> Resetting : EVT_POLL\n(interrupt == INT_RESET)
Running --> Halted : EVT_POLL\n(breakpoint hit)
Running --> WaitingForInterrupt : EVT_POLL\n(cpu.wai_state)
Running --> Halted : EVT_POLL\n(cpu.halted)
Running --> Paused : EV_PAUSE_EMULATOR
Running --> Halted : EV_CMD_HALT
Running --> Resetting : EV_CMD_RESET
Running --> Loading : EV_CMD_LOAD

Halted --> Running : EV_CMD_RUN
Halted --> Resetting : EV_CMD_RESET
Halted --> Loading : EV_CMD_LOAD

Paused --> Running : EV_RESUME_EMULATOR\n(from s_running)
Paused --> Halted : EV_RESUME_EMULATOR\n(from s_halted)
Paused --> Resetting : EV_RESUME_EMULATOR\n(from s_resetting)
Paused --> Loading : EV_RESUME_EMULATOR\n(from s_loading)
Paused --> WaitingForInterrupt : EV_RESUME_EMULATOR\n(from s_waiting_for_interrupt)

Loading --> Resetting : EV_CMD_RESET

WaitingForInterrupt --> Resetting : EVT_POLL\n(interrupt == INT_RESET)
WaitingForInterrupt --> Running : EVT_POLL\n(interrupt != INT_NONE)

note right of Initializing : Power-on initialization
note right of Resetting : Reset handling and waiting
note right of Running : Normal instruction execution
note right of Halted : Stopped (breakpoint/manual halt)
note right of Paused : USB command synchronization
note right of Loading : ROM loading operations
note right of WaitingForInterrupt : WAI instruction waiting

@enduml
